      ro: "Podișul Ozark este un element remarcabil al geografiei si culturii americane. O zonă de podiș cu păduri dense și peșteri. Regiune geologic complexă. Multe peșteri de calcar. Păduri dense de stejar și hickory. Aceasta forma de relief modeleaza topografia SUA — intre Muntii Stancosi, Muntii Apalasi, bazinul Mississippi si vastele Mari Campii. Asemenea multor locuri importante din SUA, acesta imbina particularitatile regionale cu semnificatia nationala — de la mostenirea industriala si agricultura Vestului Mijlociu pana la centrele IT din jurul Silicon Valley. Astfel, acest loc contribuie la profilul variat al Statelor Unite.",
      en: "The Ozark Plateau, often simply referred to as the Ozarks, is a heavily forested, deeply eroded massive high plateau region spanning northern Arkansas, southern Missouri, and extending into Oklahoma. While visually resembling heavily rugged mountains, the geology is technically a massive, highly uplifted plateau that has been deeply, relentlessly carved by streams over millions of years, creating incredibly steep, massive valleys and narrow ridges. The region is globally famous for its highly complex karst topography, featuring an incredibly massive concentration of deep caves, large sinkholes, and incredibly powerful, massive natural freshwater springs. The deeply isolated nature of the Ozarks historically fostered a highly unique, distinct regional culture deeply tied to the rugged terrain. Geography K7 — uplifted plateaus and karst geomorphology."
