      ro: "Big Bend este un element remarcabil al geografiei si culturii americane. O zonă deșertică accidentată la marele cot al fluviului Rio Grande. Parte a ecosistemului deșertului Chihuahua. Canioane spectaculoase. Condiții extrem de aride. Aceasta forma de relief modeleaza topografia SUA — intre Muntii Stancosi, Muntii Apalasi, bazinul Mississippi si vastele Mari Campii. Asemenea multor locuri importante din SUA, acesta imbina particularitatile regionale cu semnificatia nationala — de la mostenirea industriala si agricultura Vestului Mijlociu pana la centrele IT din jurul Silicon Valley. Astfel, acest loc contribuie la profilul variat al Statelor Unite.",
      en: "The Big Bend region of West Texas is a deeply remote, incredibly vast expanse defined entirely by the massive, sweeping curve of the Rio Grande along the Mexican border. This incredibly harsh, massive environment is a highly stark showcase of extreme Chihuahuan Desert ecology, featuring visually staggering, deeply rugged topography. The region is totally dominated by the massive Chisos Mountains, an entirely isolated, incredibly sheer volcanic range rising abruptly from the deeply arid desert floor. The massive, relentlessly eroding power of the Rio Grande has sliced through massive limestone mesas to form incredibly deep, visually breathtaking vertical canyons, including Santa Elena Canyon. The massive area remains one of the most incredibly isolated, pristine dark-sky locations globally. Geography K7 — arid geomorphology and desert mountain islands."
