      ro: "Munții Olympic este un element remarcabil al geografiei si culturii americane. Un munte izolat pe peninsula Olympic. Climat foarte umed. Singurele păduri tropicale temperate din SUA. Activitate glaciară ridicată. Aceasta forma de relief modeleaza topografia SUA — intre Muntii Stancosi, Muntii Apalasi, bazinul Mississippi si vastele Mari Campii. Asemenea multor locuri importante din SUA, acesta imbina particularitatile regionale cu semnificatia nationala — de la mostenirea industriala si agricultura Vestului Mijlociu pana la centrele IT din jurul Silicon Valley. Astfel, acest loc contribuie la profilul variat al Statelor Unite.",
      en: "The Olympic Mountains represent a visually staggering, profoundly massive and heavily rugged mountain range dominating the massive Olympic Peninsula in northwestern Washington state. Geologically, they are incredibly unique, consisting not of volcanic rock, but entirely of massive, deeply scraped oceanic crust and marine sedimentary rock that was violently, heavily pushed up into a massive chaotic jumble by the relentless tectonic subduction of the Juan de Fuca plate. Their immediate, massive proximity to the Pacific Ocean causes them to intercept incredible, massive amounts of moisture, creating profoundly dense, incredibly lush temperate rainforests on their western slopes, while maintaining heavily glaciated, massive jagged alpine peaks at their center, all protected within a massive National Park. Geography K8 — accretionary wedges and orographic rain shadows."
