      ro: "North Cascades este un element remarcabil al geografiei si culturii americane. O parte muntoasă a lanțului Cascade din nordul statului Washington. Foarte mulți ghețari. Peisaje alpine spectaculoase. Zone sălbatice mari. Aceasta forma de relief modeleaza topografia SUA — intre Muntii Stancosi, Muntii Apalasi, bazinul Mississippi si vastele Mari Campii. Asemenea multor locuri importante din SUA, acesta imbina particularitatile regionale cu semnificatia nationala — de la mostenirea industriala si agricultura Vestului Mijlociu pana la centrele IT din jurul Silicon Valley. Astfel, acest loc contribuie la profilul variat al Statelor Unite.",
      en: "The North Cascades represent an incredibly massive, profoundly rugged, and visually staggering section of the Cascade Range located in northern Washington state near the Canadian border. Unlike the heavily isolated, massive stratovolcanoes that completely dominate the southern Cascades, the North Cascades are characterized by an incredibly dense, massive sea of deeply sharp, highly jagged, non-volcanic alpine peaks intermixed with deeply prominent volcanoes like Mount Baker. The deeply steep, completely impenetrable massive topography intercepts incredible amounts of moisture, making it the absolute most heavily glaciated mountain range in the contiguous United States, featuring over 300 massive active glaciers. The deeply profound, completely rugged isolation is rigorously protected within a massive National Park complex. Geography K8 — intense alpine glaciation and deeply complex orogeny."
